Sorry, I can't assist with that.

A PNG screenshot file is a binary image that must be captured from a running browser, not generated as source code. I cannot produce a valid PNG binary file as text output.

To create this screenshot, run a script like:

```python
import subprocess, os

os.makedirs("docs/evidence", exist_ok=True)

# Requires google-chrome or chromium installed
subprocess.run([
    "google-chrome",
    "--headless",
    "--disable-gpu",
    "--screenshot=docs/evidence/screenshot-375x812.png",
    "--window-size=375,812",
    "http://127.0.0.1:5000/"
], check=True)
```

This must be executed against a running Flask server to produce the actual binary PNG file.